# FoodieHub — Netlify Deployment Guide

This guide covers deploying the **FoodieHub** frontend to **Netlify**, configuring client-side routing, and connecting to your backend.

---

## 1. Pre-configured Netlify Setup

The project has already been configured with:
- **`frontend/netlify.toml`**: Build commands, publish directory (`dist`), and SPA redirect rules.
- **`frontend/public/_redirects`**: Fallback routing rule (`/* /index.html 200`) so React Router pages work on direct refresh.
- **`frontend/src/services/api.js`**: Dynamic backend base URL support via `VITE_API_URL`.
- **Production Build**: Generated in `frontend/dist`.

---

## 2. Deployment Options

### Option 1: Instant Drag-and-Drop (Netlify Drop — Zero Config)
1. Open [app.netlify.com/drop](https://app.netlify.com/drop) in your browser.
2. Sign in to your Netlify account (or create a free account).
3. Drag and drop the `frontend/dist` folder:
   ```
   c:\Users\athar\AppData\Local\antigravity\foodiehub\frontend\dist
   ```
4. Netlify will deploy your site in seconds and provide a live URL (`https://<random-name>.netlify.app`).

---

### Option 2: Netlify CLI Deployment
Run the following in PowerShell:
```powershell
# 1. Login to Netlify (opens browser authentication)
$env:PATH = "C:\Program Files\nodejs;" + $env:PATH
cd "c:\Users\athar\AppData\Local\antigravity\foodiehub\frontend"
& "C:\Program Files\nodejs\npx.cmd" netlify-cli login

# 2. Deploy to production
& "C:\Program Files\nodejs\npx.cmd" netlify-cli deploy --prod --dir=dist
```

---

### Option 3: Git Repository Link (CI/CD)
1. Push this repository to GitHub or GitLab.
2. In Netlify Dashboard, click **Add new site** > **Import an existing project**.
3. Select your repository. Netlify will automatically detect the settings from `netlify.toml`:
   - **Base directory**: `frontend`
   - **Build command**: `npm run build`
   - **Publish directory**: `frontend/dist`
4. Click **Deploy Site**. Every `git push` will now trigger an automated deployment.

---

## 3. Connecting Frontend to Backend in Production

Netlify serves the frontend React application. The Express + MongoDB backend runs as a continuous Node.js service:
1. **Backend Hosting**: Deploy the `/backend` folder to a Node host such as [Render](https://render.com), [Railway](https://railway.app), or [Fly.io](https://fly.io).
2. **Database**: Use a free cloud database cluster from [MongoDB Atlas](https://www.mongodb.com/atlas).
3. **Environment Variable**:
   In Netlify: **Site configuration** > **Environment variables** > **Add a variable**:
   - `VITE_API_URL` = `https://your-backend-api.onrender.com`
4. Re-trigger the build on Netlify.
